WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.267
-I do want to say
before we even start

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.234
this interview,
thank you so much.

00:00:04.234 --> 00:00:06.801
You're one of the nicest guys
that I've ever worked with.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:08.968
And you're very funny obviously
and we're going to get to

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:11.400
all of the fun jokes and stuff,
but seriously --

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.567
-You know that's bull[bleep].

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.367
I'm a dick.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:15.701
-No, you are not.

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.501
I just want to say,
you really are.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:19.133
Thank you for doing --
You did me a solid.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.634
You did an episode of
"Password."

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.934
-Yes, this Tuesday?
-This Tuesday.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.767
-Yeah, guys, wait till
you see that Keke Palmer.

00:00:25.767 --> 00:00:28.834
-That's exactly right.
That's the secret ingredient.

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:33.000
-She is a comedy alien.
-She's unbelievable, right?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.300
-She pisses me off,
she's so funny.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.634
[ Laughter ]
-Makes you mad? You're jealous?

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.801
-Yeah, at 28?
-Yeah, she's the greatest.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:41.734
-I was still like,
"I should get a keg."

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:44.868
[ Laughter ]
-She's got it figured out.

00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:48.367
-She is so funny.
-Yeah.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.534
But thank you again
for doing that.

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:50.567
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:50.567 --> 00:00:53.267
I would love to come back
and host it.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.801
Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.801 --> 00:00:56.300
-You just said
how great she was.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.968
-Oh, look at that.
They're into it.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:00:59.334
-No, they're not into it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:02.100
You keep asking them.
-This is great.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.033
-You were telling me backstage
that you just came back

00:01:05.033 --> 00:01:07.067
from London,
which I do love London.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.300
You went with the family?
-Oh, no, I didn't go.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.534
I'm just kidding.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.901
Yes. I'm sorry. Yes.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:16.934
I have cousins that got
married -- not cousins.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.701
I mean, they're cous--
They're not related.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:20.968
-Wow.
They're royalty.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:22.567
No.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:27.300
So, happy wedding,
Brendan and Hannah.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.167
Yes, it was beautiful.
It was great.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.667
British weather. It was 104.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.100
[ Audience groans ]
Yeah.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.234
I was like,
you people live like animals.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:39.400
But I drove for the first time
ever

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.934
on the left side of the road.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:42.300
-Does that make you nervous?
-Yeah.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.033
It was like training a cat.

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.934
It was all wrong.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:51.801
I felt like I was playing Grand
Theft Auto, like, with a mirror.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:55.467
[ Laughter ]
And I was so nervous.

00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:57.801
And my kids were like,
"Can you turn on the music?"

00:01:57.801 --> 00:02:00.434
I'm like, "No, I'm trying to
keep us alive."

00:02:00.434 --> 00:02:02.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.601
And then I got good at it.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:06.767
Then I was just like,
"Watch this left turn."

00:02:06.767 --> 00:02:09.334
And we're staying over here.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:12.767
So, then I feel like my final
test was I drove through

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.033
Trafalgar Square
and Piccadilly Circus.

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:17.300
-Oh, my goodness.
-I had a couple of beers.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.534
-No, no, no, that's not --

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:21.901
-Yeah, I was blasting Oasis.

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:24.234
-That's what you do in London.
Yeah, of course.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.501
How old are the kids now?

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.300
-I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.901
-Ball park.
Ball park, ball park.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.467
-They're 14 and 17.
-Yeah.

00:02:32.467 --> 00:02:35.267
-And you know what teenagers
love?

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:36.567
Sightseeing.

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.367
-No interest at all?

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:42.601
-We took them to
Stonehenge and they were like --

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:45.934
My 14-year-old was like,
"[Sarcastic] Wow.

00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:49.200
Look at this pile of rocks.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.367
Thank you.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:52.901
This is really great."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:56.234
-Wow. I see they get
their sarcasm from Dad.

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:59.801
-Then we took them
to Salisbury Cathedral.

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:01.033
See?

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.834
And it's an enormous --

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:06.067
It's a beautiful church
that the poor built.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.234
And my 14-year-old, again,
was like,

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:12.300
"I am not going in there.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.868
There is no God."
No, he didn't say that.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:16.801
But he was like,
"I don't want to go in there."

00:03:16.801 --> 00:03:21.133
And then you go in there,
and he's like -- All the former,

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:23.167
you know, cardinals
or whatever are buried there.

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:25.634
It would be like
if Lorne Michaels was buried

00:03:25.634 --> 00:03:27.968
in the "SNL" stage when he dies.

00:03:27.968 --> 00:03:32.968
So, the 14-year-old was like,
"This is --" It is.

00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:36.334
He was like, "This is very weird
that they bury people at work."

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:41.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.100
-I understand, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.667
-So he's like,
"Let's keep it moving.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:47.667
And then my 17-year-old,
he's much more --

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.501
he's mellow and he's just like,
"Dad, you always know

00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.234
how to say the wrong thing

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:53.968
at the worst time."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:58.334
And I was like,
"Yep, that's my kids."

00:03:58.334 --> 00:03:59.901
-I saw you were all over
the Internet.

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:01.734
You know I follow you
on the socials too.

00:04:01.734 --> 00:04:02.968
But you were all over
the Internet

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.701
because you did
this celebrity softball game.

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:06.400
-I did, yeah.
-At Dodger Stadium?

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:11.234
-Yeah, it was --
I thought it was just a local

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:14.601
Dodger celebrity game,
and it was not.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:15.968
It was for All-Star Weekend.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:18.267
I found out I replaced Rob Lowe.

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:21.133
So, that was a first.

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:23.033
And if you had told me when
"St. Elmo's Fire"

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.167
came out that that would happen,

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:28.334
I'd be like,
"I'm living the dream."

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.400
-You looked good, buddy.
I gotta say, I got a photo.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:31.868
-I hit a home run.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:33.601
And, oh, look. Yeah.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.601
So, this is --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:38.701
No, no. No, no, no.
-What do you mean?

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:41.701
-It was an
in-the-park home run.

00:04:41.701 --> 00:04:43.567
If you play softball,
if you just keep running,

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:45.067
someone is going
to make a mistake.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:50.033
And the ball
was flying all over the place.

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.334
I was like,
"Dreams are coming true."

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:53.868
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, man.

00:04:53.868 --> 00:04:55.601
-Look, there's a Marvel star
right there.

00:04:55.601 --> 00:05:01.200
So, I couldn't believe -- Yes,
it was better than the birth

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.434
of my kids, my marriage --
[ Audience ohs ]

00:05:03.434 --> 00:05:04.834
-That's not true.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.501
-I like how people are like,
"Oh, are you being serious?"

00:05:07.501 --> 00:05:09.734
Yes. No.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:11.734
-You heard how sarcastic
his kids turned out to be.

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.834
Yeah, of course. Yeah.

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:16.801
I will say that you're getting
buzz off that,

00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:18.267
because that was everywhere,
you and Bad Bunny,

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:21.667
I saw, were hanging out.
-Yeah, see, there you go.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.968
I'm so old, I didn't --

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.667
They were like, "Bad Bunny is
going to be there."

00:05:25.667 --> 00:05:27.334
I'm like,
"Sounds like a Funko Pop."

00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:28.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:32.467
And then he showed up --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:35.501
[ Rim shot ]
How dare you?!

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:39.534
I just want to say I just got
rim-shot by an Oscar winner.

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:40.801
-Another dream come true.

00:05:40.801 --> 00:05:42.434
-That's a dream come true
right there.

00:05:42.434 --> 00:05:43.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Another dream.

00:05:43.567 --> 00:05:46.434
The dreams keep coming true
for Joel McHale.

00:05:46.434 --> 00:05:49.901
-This is -- No, and then --

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:53.000
And then when I told
my 14-year-old, I was like,

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.167
"Do you know who Bad Bunny is?"

00:05:54.167 --> 00:05:56.000
And he was just like, "Ugh"

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.234
and then he walked
out of the room.

00:05:57.234 --> 00:06:01.033
I was like, "I guess you do."

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:03.501
-That happened, then
you're on this show, by the way,

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:04.968
which I have not seen yet.

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.033
I know I'm going to love it.

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:07.501
-Thank you for being
honest though.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.033
Because if you were like,
"I loved it"

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:11.300
and I was like, "Which part?"
you'd be like, "All of it."

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.200
[ Laughter ]
-I have not seen it yet.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:15.167
It's called "The Bear."
-Oh, that one?

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.667
-Yeah.
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:18.534
-Oh, I haven't seen
your other show either.

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:21.567
[ Laughter ]
Don't worry about it.

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:24.567
I got things to do.
I'll get around to it.

00:06:24.567 --> 00:06:27.934
A bunch of rocks and Stonehenge.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:31.067
"The Bear."
I feel like this is made for me.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.100
-You love cooking.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:33.200
-I love cooking.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.567
-I was in that show
for three minutes.

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:35.634
-I know.
It doesn't matter.

00:06:35.634 --> 00:06:36.968
You could be the star.
-I really was.

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:40.167
And I literally have gotten
more response from that

00:06:40.167 --> 00:06:43.734
than an entire year
on a sitcom on CBS.

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:45.534
[ Laughter ]
I am not kidding.

00:06:45.534 --> 00:06:46.667
-I can't wait to watch it

00:06:46.667 --> 00:06:47.968
because I know
I'm going to love it.

00:06:47.968 --> 00:06:50.234
-I play a horrible person.
-Congrats on that.

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.234
-I mean the hero.
-A hero.

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:53.501
Let's talk about
"Celebrity Beef."

00:06:53.501 --> 00:06:55.467
-"Celebrity Beef."
-This is a competition series.

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.267
You are the host.
You are the judge.

00:06:57.267 --> 00:06:58.434
