for everybody?

00:06:58.434 --> 00:07:00.501
-Yeah, this is my TED Talk.

00:07:00.501 --> 00:07:02.667
This is an important show,
as you'll see.

00:07:02.667 --> 00:07:05.367
It's very sophistica-- It's
basically celebrities cooking

00:07:05.367 --> 00:07:08.934
and yelling at each other
over some small --

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:10.901
-So it's two celebrity friends,

00:07:10.901 --> 00:07:13.667
and they just have a little --
-Some sort --

00:07:13.667 --> 00:07:15.000
Rachel Harris and Cheryl Hines
were on.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.434
-Cheryl Hines I saw a clip of.
-Yes.

00:07:16.434 --> 00:07:20.501
And Rachel Harris always
changes hotel rooms,

00:07:20.501 --> 00:07:22.667
and it really makes Cheryl mad.

00:07:22.667 --> 00:07:24.100
So, that's the extent
of the argument.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.767
It's not like,
"You killed my father."

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:29.767
-No, no, it's fun,
but it's cooking.

00:07:29.767 --> 00:07:31.367
-It's screwing around.

00:07:31.367 --> 00:07:34.734
-It's Joel McHale being quick
and funny, which you always are.

00:07:34.734 --> 00:07:35.934
I want to show a clip.

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:37.400
Here's Joel McHale
in "Celebrity Beef."

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:39.634
Take a look at this.
-Now, this looks really good.

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:41.100
What the hell did you do?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:45.567
First, it looked like some sort
